# ============================================================
#  Numbers (design §8.4). Tier words in effects (`mood +medium`,
#  `rel npc -small`) take their amount from `sizes`; challenge
#  difficulty tiers shift the DC from the expected skill at that
#  point of the run (`curve`, one value per turn, fitted by
#  `node tools/grim.js curve`). All values are tunable.
# ============================================================

@balance
desc: Size tiers are tiny, small, medium, large and huge; skills use the xp row.
sizes: health 2 4 7 12 20 | mood 2 4 7 12 20 | gold 3 8 15 30 60 | renown 1 3 6 10 16 | mana 3 6 10 16 25
  | alignment 2 4 7 12 20 | xp 1 2 4 7 12 | lore 1 1 3 5 8 | rel 1 2 4 6 10 | spark 3 6 10 15 25
difficulty: trivial -15 easy -7 medium 0 hard 8 heroic 16
# Skill XP (design §8.5): the next point costs a + b × level. Fitted so a balanced player averages about 50 at the
# end of a four-year run; "focused reaches ~95 by month 24" needs phase 3's course depth (balance alarm).
xp_cost: 1 0.02
# Rank XP needed for each promotion (Member → Officer, Officer → Captain), plus performance ≥ 70.
rank_xp: 10 25
weights: health 1 mood 1 gold 0.5 renown 0.8 mana 0.4 alignment 0 xp 1.5 rel 0.6 spark 0.4
curve: 7 9 10 11 11 12 12 13 14 15 16 16 17 18 19 21 21 22 22 23 24 25 26 26 27 28 29 30 31 32 32 33 34 35 36 36 37 37 38 39 39 40 40 40 41 41 42

# ---------------- Presets (design §8.4): named groups of effects ----------------

@preset grind
params: skill
desc: Hard work on one skill.
do:
  $skill +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset rest
desc: A real rest.
do:
  mood +medium
  health +small

@preset social
params: who
desc: Time with someone.
do:
  rel $who +small
  mood +small
  gold -tiny

@preset work
desc: Paid work.
do:
  gold +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset splurge
desc: Spending to feel better.
do:
  mood +large
  gold -medium

@preset risk
params: res
desc: A gamble: a large gain or a medium loss.
do:
  chance 50:
    $res +large
  else:
    $res -medium
